IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ssaa-overpayment-dates`
IMPORT `ssaa-overpayment`

-- Social Security (Administration) Act 1999 -- worked cases for ssaa-overpayment.l4, from the seat of the person paid.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand from
-- the deposited text (C2026C00010), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this: the person (Jo, who
-- was paid jobseeker payment while working casual shifts) and every date are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 6A, 236: a decision made by a computer is in writing and is the Secretary's; a spoken-only decision is not in writing.
#ASSERT `What is the decision about me in law` `by an officer, on paper or recorded on a computer` EQUALS `a decision in writing (s 236) of the officer who made it`
#ASSERT `What is the decision about me in law` `by the operation of a computer program the Secretary arranged to use (s 6A)` EQUALS `a decision in writing (s 236(2)) taken to be made by the Secretary (s 6A(2))`
#ASSERT `What is the decision about me in law` `by an officer, only spoken, with no written or computer record` EQUALS `not a decision in writing, as s 236(1) requires a decision of an officer to be`

-- s 83: the program cut Jo's rate on 10 March 2027 for a reason the Secretary could act on: a determination made that day.
#ASSERT `On what day is the computer's change taken to be a determination` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 10 3 2027)
-- A reason the Secretary could not act on by determination: s 83 deems nothing.
#ASSERT `On what day is the computer's change taken to be a determination` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The payment is not based on data in a computer.
#ASSERT `On what day is the computer's change taken to be a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 237: notice of the debt decision.
#ASSERT `On what day was notice of the decision given to me` `handed to me personally` (`the date` 5 3 2027) (`the date` 9 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 5 3 2027)
#ASSERT `On what day was notice of the decision given to me` `left at my last home or business address the Secretary knew` (`the date` 5 3 2027) (`the date` 9 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 5 3 2027)
-- Posted: the ordinary course of post (9 March), unless Jo proves it came on 15 March.
#ASSERT `On what day was notice of the decision given to me` `posted, prepaid, to my last postal address the Secretary knew` (`the date` 5 3 2027) (`the date` 9 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 9 3 2027)
#ASSERT `On what day was notice of the decision given to me` `posted, prepaid, to my last postal address the Secretary knew` (`the date` 5 3 2027) (`the date` 9 3 2027) TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`the date` 15 3 2027)
-- Online account, or a notice that is not of a decision: s 237 does not say.
#ASSERT `On what day was notice of the decision given to me` `another way, such as my online account` (`the date` 5 3 2027) (`the date` 9 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what day was notice of the decision given to me` `it is not a notice of a decision` (`the date` 5 3 2027) (`the date` 9 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 15 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 191A, 192-194, 198(2). Inputs: about, considered relevant, owes a debt, reasonable belief, would break Cth law.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 191A: the Secretary does not reasonably believe Jo can produce payslips from a closed employer.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 198(2): giving it would contravene a Commonwealth law.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 193: only of a person who owes a debt.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my own financial situation, as a person who owes a debt under the social security law (s 193)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my own financial situation, as a person who owes a debt under the social security law (s 193)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 194: about Jo's former partner, who owes a debt.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `where another person who owes a debt is, or that person's financial situation (s 194)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `something else` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 166(3): at the ART's request under s 166(1), s 191A does not apply, so no reasonable belief is needed for a s 192 matter.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 166 reaches only s 192; for a s 193 requirement s 191A still bars it without the belief.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my own financial situation, as a person who owes a debt under the social security law (s 193)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 198(2) still applies at the ART's request.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 192(e): a foreign social security agreement; relevant: yes; not relevant: the "if" of s 192 fails.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `another matter s 192 lists: Part 3 Division 3AA or 3A, Part 3AA or 3B, fares allowance, a foreign social security agreement, an assurance of support, or an inquiry into one of them (s 192(daa)-(e), (j), (k))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `another matter s 192 lists: Part 3 Division 3AA or 3A, Part 3AA or 3B, fares allowance, a foreign social security agreement, an assurance of support, or an inquiry into one of them (s 192(daa)-(e), (j), (k))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `another matter s 192 lists: Part 3 Division 3AA or 3A, Part 3AA or 3B, fares allowance, a foreign social security agreement, an assurance of support, or an inquiry into one of them (s 192(daa)-(e), (j), (k))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give it` `another matter s 192 lists: Part 3 Division 3AA or 3A, Part 3AA or 3B, fares allowance, a foreign social security agreement, an assurance of support, or an inquiry into one of them (s 192(daa)-(e), (j), (k))` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 196(3), (6): notice given 2 March 2027; 14 days after is 16 March 2027. Across a year end: 20 Dec 2027 -> 3 Jan 2028.
#ASSERT `The earliest day the notice may set` (`the date` 2 3 2027) EQUALS `the date` 16 3 2027
#ASSERT `The earliest day the notice may set` (`the date` 20 12 2027) EQUALS `the date` 3 1 2028

-- s 196 validity. Inputs: written, describes, how, period, officer, says s 196, given, last day, appear?, time/place/lawyer,
-- appear day, Secretary satisfied shorter.
-- A complete notice giving until 16 March (the last allowed day): valid.
#ASSERT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) FALSE
-- Until 15 March: one day short, invalid unless the Secretary was satisfied a shorter period was reasonable.
#ASSERT (NOT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) TRUE
-- It does not say it is given under s 196.
#ASSERT (NOT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) FALSE)
-- Not written.
#ASSERT (NOT `Does the notice meet s 196` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) FALSE)
-- A notice to appear on 16 March, saying Jo may bring a lawyer: valid; on 15 March: not; without the lawyer statement: not.
#ASSERT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT `Does the notice meet s 196` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE FALSE (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 197. Notice given 2 March 2027, last day 16 March 2027. Inputs: valid, given, last day, complied?, day complied, today,
-- capable, why not.
-- Complied on the last day, and on the day of the notice: no offence.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE (`the date` 16 3 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `no particular reason` EQUALS `no offence: you complied within the period the notice gives`
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `no particular reason` EQUALS `no offence: you complied within the period the notice gives`
-- Complied a day late, no excuse: the offence.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE (`the date` 17 3 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `no particular reason` EQUALS `an offence against s 197(1): imprisonment for up to 12 months`
-- Not yet complied: on the last day, still time; the day after, the offence.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) TRUE `no particular reason` EQUALS `not yet: the period the notice gives has not ended; comply by its last day`
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 17 3 2027) TRUE `no particular reason` EQUALS `an offence against s 197(1): imprisonment for up to 12 months`
-- The notice did not meet s 196.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` FALSE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `no particular reason` EQUALS `s 197 does not apply: the requirement was not made by a notice that meets s 196`
-- The excuses, after the period.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `complying would break a Commonwealth law` EQUALS `no offence: this Division does not require you to break a Commonwealth law (s 198(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) FALSE `no particular reason` EQUALS `no offence to the extent you were not capable of complying (s 197(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `another reason that may be a reasonable excuse` EQUALS `no offence if you have a reasonable excuse (s 197(3)); whether the excuse is reasonable is for the court`
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by not complying` TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 20 3 2027) TRUE `it might incriminate me or expose me to a penalty` EQUALS `an offence against s 197(1), imprisonment for up to 12 months: fear of self-incrimination or a penalty is no excuse (s 197A(1)), though what you give cannot be used against you in most criminal proceedings (s 197A(2))`

-- s 197A(2), 197B.
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `criminal proceedings for not complying with the requirement (s 197(1))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `criminal proceedings for false or misleading information or documents (Criminal Code s 137.1 or 137.2) relating to the requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `criminal proceedings for an offence in Criminal Code Division 145 (using forged documents and related offences)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `criminal proceedings under s 217 for a false statement or document (s 212(1), 213(1), 214(1), 214(2) or 216(3)) relating to the requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `other criminal proceedings against me` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `an inquiry or investigation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can what I give be used against me` `civil proceedings, such as recovering a debt` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 193(b): Jo, who owes a debt, moved on 1 April 2027; 14 days after is 15 April 2027.
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Department my new address in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the date` 15 4 2027) (`the date` 20 4 2027) EQUALS `in time: you told the Department within 14 days after the change`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Department my new address in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the date` 16 4 2027) (`the date` 20 4 2027) EQUALS `late: you did not tell the Department within 14 days after the change, as the requirement asks`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Department my new address in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 15 4 2027) EQUALS `still in time: tell the Department within 14 days after the change`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Department my new address in time` TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 16 4 2027) EQUALS `late: you did not tell the Department within 14 days after the change, as the requirement asks`
#ASSERT `Did I tell the Department my new address in time` FALSE (`the date` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 30 4 2027) EQUALS `s 193(b) does not apply: no notice required you to tell the Department of a change of address`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 195(2): the closed list. Jo's employer may be asked for its payments to Jo in the past 52 weeks ((h)) and Jo's start
-- and end dates ((j)), but not Jo's hours.
#ASSERT `Can a body be made to give this about me under s 195` `payments the body gave me in the 52 weeks before the notice, and the account they were paid into (s 195(2)(h))`
#ASSERT `Can a body be made to give this about me under s 195` `the start and end dates of my employment with the body asked (s 195(2)(j))`
#ASSERT `Can a body be made to give this about me under s 195` `my name, address, sex, marital status, date of birth or death, or my entries to and departures from Australia (s 195(2)(a)-(g))`
#ASSERT `Can a body be made to give this about me under s 195` `my income stream: the items s 195(2)(ja) lists`
#ASSERT (NOT `Can a body be made to give this about me under s 195` `anything else, such as my hours worked or my bank balance`)

-- s 195(4): given 1 March 2027; 13 weeks (91 days) after is 31 May 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary decide on the s 195 information` (`the date` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `the date` 31 5 2027
-- s 195(5), (6).
#ASSERT `Must the s 195 record about me be destroyed` (`the date` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 4 2027)
#ASSERT (NOT `Must the s 195 record about me be destroyed` (`the date` 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 4 2027))
#ASSERT (NOT `Must the s 195 record about me be destroyed` (`the date` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 31 5 2027))
#ASSERT `Must the s 195 record about me be destroyed` (`the date` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 6 2027)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 212-216. Inputs: what, false or misleading, reckless as to falsity, reckless as to deceiving or rate, knew not payable.
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `made a statement in connection with, or in support of, my or another person's claim, or a hardship request under 1991 Act s 1129 or 1131 (s 212)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Jo's statement was wrong, but Jo was not reckless: no contravention.
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `made a statement in connection with, or in support of, my or another person's claim, or a hardship request under 1991 Act s 1129 or 1131 (s 212)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `made a statement (s 213)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `made a statement (s 213)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `presented a document to an officer or Services Australia (s 214(2))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `made a statement to an officer or Services Australia (s 214(1))` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `obtained a payment or instalment (s 215)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `obtained a payment or instalment (s 215)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `obtained a payment or instalment by impersonation or a fraudulent device (s 216(1))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `obtained a payment or instalment as a result of a statement I made (s 216(3))` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` `obtained a payment or instalment as a result of a statement I made (s 216(3))` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ss 217-219, 233: three offences, $12,000 paid because of them: 36 months in all, repayment up to $12,000, no gaol for
-- not paying it. Convicted only through an agent's conduct: no imprisonment.
#ASSERT (`The most a court can order me` 3 12000 FALSE)'s `most months of imprisonment in all` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`The most a court can order me` 3 12000 FALSE)'s `most repayment the court can order` EQUALS 12000
#ASSERT (NOT (`The most a court can order me` 3 12000 FALSE)'s `I can be imprisoned for not paying it`)
#ASSERT (`The most a court can order me` 1 4500 FALSE)'s `most months of imprisonment in all` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT (`The most a court can order me` 2 4500 TRUE)'s `most months of imprisonment in all` EQUALS 0

